    "todo": [
        "Confirm (accountant) every class, then publish it as confirmed through a pack release (ADM-04). Medium confidence (owner decision 2026-10-22): the consolidated Act (Kenya Law, 2026-07-01) and PwC agree. The acquisition rule is low confidence.",
        "buildings: commercial buildings 10% straight line. Hotels, buildings used for manufacture, hospitals and petroleum or gas storage take 50% in the first year then 25% of the residue; educational and industrial buildings and docks 10%. Use another class key for those when a company has them.",
        "machinery: machinery used for manufacture (also hospital equipment, ships, aircraft): 50% in the first year of use, then 25% a year of the residue in equal instalments. Some summaries call the 25% reducing balance; the Act says equal instalments.",
        "motor_vehicles: 25% straight line (heavy earth-moving equipment too); the cost of a non-commercial vehicle is capped at KES 3 million (para 6), not applied.",
        "computers and software: 25% straight line (computers, peripheral hardware and software, calculators, copiers).",
        "furniture: furniture and fittings 10% straight line. telecommunication: 10% straight line. other: other machinery 10% straight line.",
        "Not modelled: the 100% investment deduction (para 1A thresholds), filming equipment 25%, exploration machinery and farm works 50% then 25%, fibre-optic IRU and spectrum licences 10%.",
        "acquisition_rule: full year assumed. The Act gives each rate 'for each year of income' ('50% in the first year of use') and no time apportionment was found; this is a reading of the law, not a stated rule.",
        "Disposals: the balancing allowance or charge in the year of disposal (paras 3 and 4; until confirmed the tax book gives no allowance that year and computes no balancing adjustment)."
    ],
